cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Multi-Turn Distributed Prompt Injection Detection"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lambros
    given-names: Rock
    email: rock@rockcyber.com
date-released: "2026-05-17"
url: "https://github.com/rocklambros/multiturn-injection-detection"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rocklambros/multiturn-injection-detection"
license: CC-BY-NC-4.0
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - multi-turn
  - deep-learning
  - nlp
  - security
  - gru
  - lstm
  - attention
abstract: >-
  A deep learning system that detects prompt injection attacks distributed
  across multiple conversation turns. Compares a lightweight dual-encoder
  architecture (frozen GRU turn encoder + trainable LSTM sequence classifier,
  27K parameters, F1=0.837 on shared-prefix evaluation) against fully
  fine-tuned DistilBERT (66.4M parameters, F1=0.992). Demonstrates that
  temporal modeling significantly outperforms per-turn classification
  (p < 0.001) and that turn order carries genuine discriminative signal.
